Z||000009||Standard||03-17-2001||11:28 PM||||Looks great man!  One thing, though - try to keep at least 12 inches between the RCA patch cords and the power cable.  You'll get better sound and less interference(sp).||||reg||1
Z||000010||sqoach||03-18-2001||03:10 PM||||it sure does sound nice. i did happen to find a rattle though. since it is right under the a/c duct, it rattles the blower motor. so i might get some rubber washers to put under the the screws. and if that doesn't work, guess i'll try something else.<P>thanks for the comments, guys. if i did build one again, with the speaker facing toward the console, i would have to go with an 8" sub. like i mentioned earlier, it would work out a lot better and not stick out so far. that's the only drawback.<P>stimpy, that's about what i was thinking for a price. i don't know if i'll get into doing that though. unless a few people liked my design then i may consider it.<P>standard, where did you run your patch cord? i was first considering running it under the lower door trim, but didn't have time that day i put it all in.||||reg||10
